Wait appending after `animate();` top-level works. Reload page. Then open slicer, start, spawn all types maybe pause? We can spawn in a ring with forced type and set positions? spawnSlicerObject only from bottom. We can call spawn many types; they launch up. We can even modify slicer.objects positions after spawn via debug. We'll call:
```
const d=window.__slicerDebug; d.startSlicerRun(); d.slicer.objects.length=0; 
['xwing','tie','vader','protocol','destroyer','darksaber','seismic','bomb','charge'].forEach((t,i)=>d.spawnSlicerObject(0,t));
// then set positions manually across screen and vy 0 maybe
d.slicer.objects.forEach((o,i)=>{o.x=...; o.y=...; o.vy=...; o.vx=0});
```
But animate will keep updating and gravity; screenshot immediately. Could set y positions in grid and velocity to hover? We can set `slicer.running=false` to pause after spawn then positions static, but draw loop continues? `slicerLoop` runs while open. updateSlicer still moves objects even if running false? The physics loop always runs regardless. Set gravity? constant. Could set each object.vy = -? They will move. We can take screenshot quickly. Or set `slicer.objects` and then screenshot within 1 frame? playwright screenshot after eval takes ~500ms; gravity would drop them 150px. Could set vy = -500 to counter? Hmm.

Better create a separate function in debug that lays out objects stationary by overriding `updateSlicer` impossible. We can set `slicer.paused`? no.

Simplest: spawn each type from bottom at intervals and screenshot after 0.8s; they'll be mid-air in a cluster. But all overlap.

We can set positions manually and screenshot immediately using a single eval that returns after requestAnimationFrame? The CLI `eval` then screenshot call has latency. Objects fall ~0.5*1180*0.25=147px in 0.5s. If we set vy = -1180*0.25 = -295, after .5s they'll be near same. Yes set vy = -250 and vx=0, positions grid; y will rise then fall. At screenshot ~0.5s later, y decreases ~? displacement -125 + 147 = +22, close. Good. Let's set grid positions at y=300..500 and screenshot. Use `eval` to set.

Need navigate. Reload page, open activities and slicer. Use click. Then eval.

